<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">The Dealer Flywheel Method</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px);">Nine steps, run in order, every time.</h1>
    <p class="sub">The last step is the point of the name. One implementation shows you the next opportunity, and the store compounds rather than starting over.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">01</div><h3>MAP</h3><p>People, processes, systems and data. We learn how work actually happens, not how the org chart says it does.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">02</div><h3>FIND</h3><p>Revenue leakage, duplicate work, slow response, missed follow-up, software you pay for but barely use.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">03</div><h3>PRIORITIZE</h3><p>Every opportunity scored on impact, feasibility, cost, risk and whether your people will actually adopt it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">04</div><h3>DESIGN</h3><p>Workflow, AI and integration architecture, with human approval points, escalation rules and a measurement plan.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">05</div><h3>BUILD</h3><p>Agents, automations, APIs, CRM workflows, dashboards and internal tools. We build it, not just recommend it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">06</div><h3>DEPLOY</h3><p>Into production, with a rollout plan. Not an email containing a login and good luck.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">07</div><h3>TRAIN</h3><p>Managers, BDC, sales, service, marketing and admin, with documentation that stays behind when we leave.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">08</div><h3>MEASURE</h3><p>Baseline, KPI, adoption, result. If it didn't move, we say so and change it.</p></div>
      <div class="step last"><div class="n">09</div><h3>FLYWHEEL</h3><p>The result exposes the next opportunity, and the cycle runs again. That's the whole business model.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="journey">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">What we actually do</p>
        <h2>The same lead, with the breaks fixed.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">A failed lead is not unusual, and every place it fell down is a place something can be built. This is the map we work from.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="jrn">
      <div class="jhd"><div>Stage</div><div>Where it breaks today</div><div>What we implement</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Inquiry</span></div><div class="jbrk">A form arrives at 9 p.m. on a Saturday.</div><div class="jfix">Acknowledge in seconds, at any hour</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Routing</span></div><div class="jbrk">Duplicate record, wrong salesperson.</div><div class="jfix">Classify and route on arrival</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">First response</span></div><div class="jbrk">Hours pass, not minutes.</div><div class="jfix">Response drafted instantly, a person sends it</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Follow-up</span></div><div class="jbrk">Two attempts, then it stops.</div><div class="jfix">Sequenced follow-up that doesn't quit</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">05</span><span class="t">Appointment</span></div><div class="jbrk">Set, but never confirmed.</div><div class="jfix">Confirmation and reminder workflow</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">06</span><span class="t">Sale</span></div><div class="jbrk">Only the salesperson knows what happened.</div><div class="jfix">Deal summary written back to the CRM</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">07</span><span class="t">Service</span></div><div class="jbrk">Declined work is never revisited.</div><div class="jfix">Declined-work recovery outreach</div></div>
      <div class="jrw"><div class="jstg"><span class="n">08</span><span class="t">Retention</span></div><div class="jbrk">Nobody reaches back out.</div><div class="jfix">Maintenance and win-back campaigns</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="jloop">Service and retention create the next inquiry, and the sequence starts again. That is the flywheel the company is named for.</p>
    <p class="jnote">Every step keeps a human approval point — we build the workflow, your people decide where it may act on its own. A first engagement fixes one of these, not all eight; which one depends on what the diagnostic finds in your store.</p>
  </div>
</section>

